To Whom It May Concern:

Subject: STATE CONSTABLE GLENN MARKLEY Records Request - Constable Vendor Financial Records & Audit Trail

Pursuant to the Pennsylvania Right-to-Know Law (65 P.S. § 67.101 et seq.), I hereby request copies of specific financial records documenting the expenditure of public funds to the constable vendor identified below;

About Samuel Glenn Markley (aka GLENN MARKLEY) or any PERSON he uses (e.g. INCARCERATE INC, "0000033488 Incarcerate, Inc.") provide specific financial records for periods of dates including:
A. April 9th of 2024 through May 14th of 2024, 
B. June 18th of 2024 through August 6th of 2024,
C. September 23rd of 2025 through November 18th of 2025,
D. January 27th of 2026 through April 11th of 2026;

This request is strictly for fiscal and administrative records held by the Chester County Controller’s Office regarding vendor payment processing, auditing, and disbursement; these records constitute "financial records" and "expenditure reports" under Section 102 of the RTKL;  judicial case files, court opinions, investigative notes, or records protected by Pa.R.J.A. No. 509 are not being requested at this time; to the extent any document contains sensitive personal information, this request includes that only defendant names be redacted, while docket numbers, fees, dates, and service descriptions remain visible as they are essential financial line-item descriptors;;;

Specific Records Requested: This request is for electronic copies (PDF) of the following documents, using the exact titles as they appear in the Chester County Constable Handbook and Controller’s Office records:

A. Original Executed Payment Sheets (Invoices): 1. all Criminal Payment Sheets and Civil Payment Sheets submitted by the named constable during the dates, 2. all Children, Youth and Families Payment Forms and Juvenile Transport Payment Sheets, 3. requirement includes that these records must be the original executed copies containing both the Constable’s signature and the Magisterial District Judge’s (MDJ) signature in the Verification section—do not provide unsigned drafts, data exports, or summaries;

B. Recapitulation Sheets: all Criminal Recapitulation Sheets and Civil Recapitulation Sheets submitted by the constable to group the above Payment Sheets;

C. Server Fee Notices: all Server Fee Notices (Treasurer’s Copies) associated with the requested Payment Sheets, showing the fees assessed by the court;

D. Internal Accounts Payable Vouchers: all Accounts Payable Vouchers created by the Controller’s Office corresponding to each approved Payment Sheet, showing the assigned Voucher Number, general ledger codes, and approved amount;

E. Payment Registers and Check Logs: the specific pages from the Check Register or Payment Log showing the Check Numbers (or EFT Trace Numbers), Payment Dates, Vendor Payment ID, and the specific list of Voucher Numbers consolidated into each payment;

F. Canceled Checks / EFT Confirmations: images of the front and back of all Canceled Checks or electronic transfer confirmations issued to this vendor for the requested dates;

G. Audit and Adjustment Documentation: any internal memos, emails, Audit Correction Notes, or correspondence between the Controller’s Office, the Constable, or the MDJ regarding adjustments, reductions, denials, or queries about the requested Payment Sheets;;;

Format And Redaction Instructions: 

A. Format—this request is for these records in electronic format (PDF),  if records exist only in paper format, provide written instructions on how to inspect and copy them at your office;

B. Do Not Redact: Docket Numbers, Case Numbers, Dates of Service, Type of Service, Mileage Claims, Fees Charged, Vendor Name, or Signatures—these are essential financial data points required to audit the expenditure of public funds;

C. May Redact: Defendant Names and Plaintiff Names (if strictly required for privacy), provided the Docket Number remains visible to allow cross-referencing with public court records;

D. Per Office of Open Records precedent, docket numbers on financial invoices are public financial descriptors, not confidential judicial deliberations—redacting them prevents the public from verifying if the billed service corresponds to a public court record, violating the core purpose of the RTKL;;;

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

If any portion of this request is denied, please provide a written denial citing the specific legal authority and exemption under the RTKL or Pa.R.J.A.  No. 509 for each withheld record, as required by 65 P.S. § 67.903.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 5 business days, as the statute requires.


Sincerely,

David Murray High
